<section class="settings-section panel" id="telegram">
    <div class="settings-copy"><span class="eyebrow">05 · Telegram</span><h2>One bot for notifications and stock questions</h2><p>The local Telegram Hub sends alerts and reports, then accepts tickers or company names such as <code>/stock NVDA</code>, <code>/stock NVIDIA</code>, <code>Apple</code>, <code>what about Tesla?</code>, or <code>what's new with NVIDIA?</code>. Explicit <code>/stock</code> requests use the immediate factual path. Natural questions use the AI chat path with the same live quote context and automatically fall back to the factual answer if AI is unavailable.</p><div class="notice info">Telegram is polled once per minute, so a normal reply should arrive within about 60 seconds while both WAMP and Docker Desktop are running.</div><div class="verification <?= !empty($settings['telegram_verified'])?'verified':'unverified' ?>"><span><?= !empty($settings['telegram_verified'])?'✓':'!' ?></span><div><strong><?= !empty($settings['telegram_verified'])?'Connection verified':'Not verified' ?></strong><small>Last test <?= e($settings['last_test_at']??'never') ?> · <?= e($settings['last_test_status']??'not run') ?></small></div></div></div>
